>>
endobj
751 0 obj
<<
/Title (Replaceable Hardware Means Cloneable Hardware Since FPGAs can be replaced, cloned or counterfeited, there is a growing need to verify the identity of a device before it is trusted.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 666 0 R
/Prev 750 0 R
/First 819 0 R
/Last 819 0 R
/Count -1
>>
endobj
752 0 obj
<<
/Title (Existing authentication methods often depend on stored secret keys, which can be copied or extracted from device memory. There is a need for a hardware-based authentication mechanism that uniquely identifies each FPGA device, using a fingerprint that is difficult to clone, requires no permanently stored secret key, and remains reliable despite minor environmental variations.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 667 0 R
/Next 820 0 R
>>
endobj
753 0 obj
<<
/Title (Design and implement an FPGA-based hardware authentication framework using Ring Oscillator PUF to uniquely identify FPGA devices and evaluate its reliability using statistical performance metrics.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 667 0 R
/Prev 821 0 R
>>
